VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  LambdaCDM's own halo scaling predicts a RISING RAR scale, x1.5-1.8 by z=2 and x2.4-3 by z=2.3-3 (analytic), matching Magneticum's x3 and
  MUSE's x2.4 at z~1: the MUSE rise is LambdaCDM-native.  The framework's derived law is FLAT to z=5.  If the flat law is what the clean
  (BTFR / massive-disk) arm shows at z=2-3, LambdaCDM must change the FABRIC: inner-halo dilution c_req/c_Nbody ~ (H/H0)^(-2/3) (0.85 at z=1,
  0.61 at z=2, 0.40 at z=3, 0.12 at z=5 -- rho_s at 2% of N-body), an H(z)-locked property gravity-only halos lack and feedback does not
  supply; the CPL law has no NFW solution at z=5.  That is the CRISPY mechanism prediction, both ways:
  a rising BTFR zero-point at z>=2 favours LambdaCDM-native structure and kills the framework's flat law; a flat one forces the fabric change.

